html.gadget/--datasheet--                            html.gadget/--datasheet--

   NAME
    html.gadget  -- display simple HTML 4 documents

   SUPERCLASS
    gadgetclass

   REQUIREMENTS
    AmigaOS 3.2 (intuition, graphics and utility V39+; window.class and
    layout.gadget V47 for ReAction use), datatypes.library for pictures.

   DESCRIPTION
    html.gadget is a ReAction/BOOPSI gadget that parses and displays simple
    HTML 4 documents: formatted text, lists, tables, links and pictures (via
    datatypes). Text is drawn with the system's bitmap fonts; bigger HTML
    font sizes use the nearest size that exists as a real bitmap font, so no
    scaled fonts are used. Rendering goes through an off-screen bitmap, so
    scrolling does not flicker.

   METHODS
    OM_NEW, OM_SET, OM_UPDATE, OM_GET, OM_DISPOSE, GM_DOMAIN, GM_LAYOUT,
    GM_RENDER, GM_HITTEST, GM_GOACTIVE, GM_HANDLEINPUT, GM_GOINACTIVE,
    HTMLM_Export, HTMLM_PrintBegin, HTMLM_PrintRender, HTMLM_PrintEnd (V1.2).
    All other methods are passed to the superclass.

   ATTRIBUTES
    HTML_Text, HTML_File, HTML_Title, HTML_Top, HTML_Total, HTML_Visible,
    HTML_Left, HTML_TotalWidth, HTML_VisibleWidth, HTML_LinkURL, HTML_Anchor,
    HTML_SystemColors, HTML_Margin, HTML_LineHeight, HTML_AutoAnchors,
    HTML_FitImages, HTML_Frame, HTML_NumLinks, HTML_BaseDir, HTML_LoadImages,
    HTML_ImagesTotal, HTML_ImagesLoaded, HTML_ImageError, HTML_Copy,
    HTML_SelectAll, HTML_ClearSelection, HTML_HasSelection,
    HTML_SelectedText

   SUPPORTED HTML
    <html> <head> <title> <body bgcolor text link vlink alink background>
    <p> <br> <div> <center> <h1>..<h6> <hr> <pre> <xmp> <listing>
    <blockquote> <address> <b> <strong> <i> <em> <u> <s> <strike> <tt>
    <code> <kbd> <samp> <var> <cite> <dfn> <big> <small> <sub> <sup> <q>
    <nobr> <font size color face> <a href name> <ul> <ol> <li> <dl> <dt>
    <dd> <table> <caption> <tr> <td> <th> (colspan, rowspan, width, align, valign,
    bgcolor, border, cellpadding, cellspacing, nowrap, background) <img>
    (align=left/right floats with text flowing around it, hspace, vspace,
    <br clear>) <input> (as boxes; checkboxes and radio buttons with their
    state, read only). Entities of HTML 4 Latin-1 plus numeric
    entities; UTF-8 input is detected and converted to Latin-1. Not
    supported: CSS, JavaScript, frames, rowspan, floating tables.

   STACK
    The gadget swaps to its own stack of 64 KB for the work that needs much
    of it: parsing, layout, the FreeType output of htmlttf.gadget and
    HTMLM_Export. Intuition may call the gadget on the input.device task,
    whose stack is small.

    Other work runs on the stack of the calling task: setting HTML_File or
    HTML_Text (OM_NEW, OM_SET) loads the pictures through datatypes.library
    (picture.datatype and the format datatypes) and opens the fonts with
    diskfont.library; window.class and layout.gadget add their own needs.
    The application should therefore run with at least 16 KB of stack,
    32 KB are recommended. Too little stack typically ends in a crash
    while the document or its pictures are loaded (e.g. software error
    80000003 or 80000004).

    Started from the Workbench, a program gets the stack of its icon; a
    program without its own icon (default tool icon) gets only 4 KB. From
    the Shell the "Stack" command sets it. The application can make sure of
    its stack in the code, independent of how it is started:

      - libnix (bebbo's amiga-gcc, -noixemul): define

            unsigned long __stack = 32768;

        and link with -Wl,-u,___stkinit; the startup code then swaps to a
        stack of this size if the current one is smaller (HTMLDemo does so).
      - SAS/C: "long __stack = 32768;" is honoured by the startup code.
      - Any compiler: allocate a stack and call the GUI code through
        exec.library/StackSwap(), as the gadget does itself.

   USAGE
    Link clicks are reported with IDCMP_GADGETUP (WMHI_GADGETUP), Code =
    index of the link; read HTML_LinkURL for the target. Scrollers are
    connected with ICA_TARGET/ICA_MAP: HTML_Top/HTML_Total/HTML_Visible to a
    vertical scroller, SCROLLER_Top back to HTML_Top (see the demo source).
    Text is selected by dragging with the left mouse button, a double click
    selects a word; HTML_Copy puts the selection into the clipboard.

   EXAMPLE
        struct Library *HTMLBase = OpenLibrary("gadgets/html.gadget", 1);
        Object *html = NewObject(HTML_GetClass(), NULL,
            GA_ID,        1,
            GA_RelVerify, TRUE,
            HTML_File,    "PROGDIR:help.html",
            TAG_DONE);

   SEE ALSO
    gadgets/html.h, Demo/HTMLDemo.c
html.gadget/HTMLM_Export                              html.gadget/HTMLM_Export

   NAME
    HTMLM_Export -- write the document as PostScript or PDF (V1.2)

   SYNOPSIS
    LONG pages = DoMethod(obj, HTMLM_Export, struct TagItem *tags);

   FUNCTION
    Lays the document out again for the paper and writes it to a DOS file
    handle: PostScript (level 1, the page size is set with setpagedevice
    where available) or PDF 1.4. The standard PostScript fonts are used
    (Helvetica or Times for text, Courier for <pre>, <tt> etc.), so text
    stays text and no fonts are embedded; the characters are ISO-8859-1.
    Pictures are included with their original pixels (PDF: with their
    transparency), tiled background pictures are not printed. Pages are
    broken where no text line, picture or rule is cut, a heading stays
    with the text after it.

    Call it with DoMethod() from the application's process, not with
    DoGadgetMethod(). The window may stay open meanwhile; the gadget is
    locked until the method returns.

   TAGS
    HTMLEX_File (BPTR) - the output, opened with MODE_NEWFILE; a file,
        PRT: or a PostScript handler. Required.
    HTMLEX_Format (ULONG) - HTMLEXF_PS (default) or HTMLEXF_PDF.
    HTMLEX_PaperWidth, HTMLEX_PaperHeight (LONG) - paper size in points
        (1/72 inch), default A4 (595 x 842).
    HTMLEX_MarginLeft, HTMLEX_MarginTop, HTMLEX_MarginRight,
    HTMLEX_MarginBottom (LONG) - margins in points, default 57 (20 mm).
    HTMLEX_FontSize (LONG) - size of normal text in 1/10 points, default
        100 (10 pt); headings and <font size> scale with it.
    HTMLEX_Serif (BOOL) - text in Times instead of Helvetica.
    HTMLEX_Backgrounds (BOOL) - print background colours (default TRUE).
    HTMLEX_Footer (STRPTR) - centred text in the bottom margin, %p is
        replaced with the page number, %n with the number of pages, e.g.
        "%p / %n". Default: none.
    HTMLEX_Title (STRPTR) - title for the PDF document information and
        the PostScript header, default the document's <title>.
    HTMLEX_FirstPage, HTMLEX_LastPage (LONG) - range of pages to write,
        counted from 1; default all.
    HTMLEX_ProgressHook (struct Hook *) - called before every page with
        the gadget as object and a struct HTMLExportProgress (Page, Pages)
        as message; return non-zero to stop.
    HTMLEX_Pages (LONG *) - receives the number of pages of the document.

   RESULT
    pages - the number of pages written, 0 if the page range was empty,
        -1 on an error (IoErr() tells: write error, ERROR_NO_FREE_STORE,
        ERROR_REQUIRED_ARG_MISSING without HTMLEX_File), -2 if the
        progress hook stopped it.

   SEE ALSO
    gadgets/html.h, Demo/HTMLDemo.c
html.gadget/HTMLM_PrintBegin                      html.gadget/HTMLM_PrintBegin

   NAME
    HTMLM_PrintBegin -- lay the document out for bitmap printing (V1.2)

   SYNOPSIS
    LONG pages = DoMethod(obj, HTMLM_PrintBegin, struct TagItem *tags);

   FUNCTION
    Prepares the pages of the document as pixels of the whole sheet. The
    document is laid out for the paper with the gadget's bitmap fonts, at
    the resolution that fits their size: the line height of the normal
    font corresponds to 1.2 times HTMLEX_FontSize. HTMLEX_DPI is ignored;
    HTMLEX_PageWidth/Height tell the size of the sheet in pixels, and the
    printer driver scales the pages to the paper. The result is as coarse
    as the fonts; htmlttf.gadget prints in the resolution of the printer.

    The pages are drawn as on the screen, with the screen's pens and the
    pictures remapped for it, so the gadget must have been shown (a
    GM_RENDER) on a screen that is still open while printing. Margins are
    white, HTMLEX_Footer is drawn centred in the bottom margin, tiled
    background pictures are not printed.

    A new HTMLM_PrintBegin, setting a new document or disposing the gadget
    frees an earlier print layout.

   TAGS
    HTMLEX_PaperWidth, HTMLEX_PaperHeight, HTMLEX_MarginLeft,
    HTMLEX_MarginTop, HTMLEX_MarginRight, HTMLEX_MarginBottom,
    HTMLEX_FontSize, HTMLEX_Backgrounds, HTMLEX_Footer - as for
        HTMLM_Export.
    HTMLEX_Pages (LONG *) - receives the number of pages.
    HTMLEX_PageWidth, HTMLEX_PageHeight (LONG *) - receive the size of
        the sheet in pixels.

   RESULT
    pages - the number of pages, -1 without memory or document, or if the
        gadget has not been shown yet.

   SEE ALSO
    HTMLM_PrintRender, HTMLM_PrintEnd, HTMLM_Export,
    htmlttf.gadget/HTMLM_PrintBegin, printer.device/PRD_DUMPRPORTTAGS,
    Demo/HTMLDemo.c
html.gadget/HTMLM_PrintEnd                          html.gadget/HTMLM_PrintEnd

   NAME
    HTMLM_PrintEnd -- free the print layout (V1.2)

   SYNOPSIS
    DoMethod(obj, HTMLM_PrintEnd);

   FUNCTION
    Frees what HTMLM_PrintBegin set up. Nothing happens without it.

   SEE ALSO
    HTMLM_PrintBegin
html.gadget/HTMLM_PrintRender                    html.gadget/HTMLM_PrintRender

   NAME
    HTMLM_PrintRender -- pixels of a rectangle of a page (V1.2)

   SYNOPSIS
    BOOL ok = DoMethod(obj, HTMLM_PrintRender, LONG page, LONG x, LONG y,
                       LONG width, LONG height, ULONG *buffer);

   FUNCTION
    Fills buffer with width * height pixels 0x00RRGGBB, row by row, of the
    rectangle x/y/width/height (in pixels of the sheet, see
    HTMLEX_PageWidth/Height) of page 'page' (from 1). This is the format
    of struct DRPSourceMsg, so a DRPA_SourceHook can pass its buffer on.
    The rectangle is drawn into a bitmap of the screen's format and read
    back (cybergraphics.library on RTG screens, else the colour map).

    It may be called from another task, e.g. printer.device's; it works on
    a stack of its own and locks the gadget meanwhile.

   RESULT
    ok - FALSE without HTMLM_PrintBegin or without memory.

   SEE ALSO
    HTMLM_PrintBegin
html.gadget/HTML_Anchor                                html.gadget/HTML_Anchor

   NAME
    HTML_Anchor -- (STRPTR) scroll to a named anchor (V1)

   USAGE
    (OM_SET)

   FUNCTION
    Scrolls to <a name="..."> or an element with id="...". A leading '#' is
    ignored. If the gadget has not been laid out yet, the jump is done at the
    next layout.
html.gadget/HTML_AutoAnchors                      html.gadget/HTML_AutoAnchors

   NAME
    HTML_AutoAnchors -- (BOOL) handle "#anchor" links internally (V1)

   USAGE
    (OM_NEW, OM_SET, OM_GET)

   FUNCTION
    If TRUE (default), clicking a link whose HREF starts with '#' scrolls to
    that anchor. A GADGETUP is sent in any case.
html.gadget/HTML_BaseDir                              html.gadget/HTML_BaseDir

   NAME
    HTML_BaseDir -- (STRPTR) directory of the last HTML_File (V1)

   USAGE
    (OM_GET)

   FUNCTION
    The path part of the file loaded with HTML_File, "" after HTML_Text.
    Use it to resolve relative links (AddPart()).
html.gadget/HTML_ClearSelection                html.gadget/HTML_ClearSelection

   NAME
    HTML_ClearSelection -- (BOOL) remove the text selection (V1)

   USAGE
    (OM_SET)
html.gadget/HTML_Copy                                    html.gadget/HTML_Copy

   NAME
    HTML_Copy -- (BOOL) copy the selection to the clipboard (V1)

   USAGE
    (OM_SET) -- application's process only

   FUNCTION
    Writes the selected text as IFF FTXT/CHRS to clipboard unit 0. Wrapped
    lines of a paragraph are joined with blanks, table columns are separated
    by TAB, blocks by LF. Typical use: menu item "Copy" (Amiga-C).

   SEE ALSO
    HTML_SelectedText, HTML_HasSelection
html.gadget/HTML_File                                    html.gadget/HTML_File

   NAME
    HTML_File -- (STRPTR) load an HTML file (V1)

   USAGE
    (OM_NEW, OM_SET) -- application's process only

   FUNCTION
    Loads and displays the file. Pictures are loaded relative to its
    directory, see HTML_BaseDir. The scroll position is reset to the top.
html.gadget/HTML_FitImages                          html.gadget/HTML_FitImages

   NAME
    HTML_FitImages -- (BOOL) scale wide pictures down to the text width (V1.2)

   USAGE
    (OM_NEW, OM_SET, OM_GET)

   FUNCTION
    If TRUE, a picture wider than the space it is in is scaled down to that
    width, keeping its proportions - like "max-width: 100%" in CSS. The space
    is the text width of the gadget (its width minus HTML_Margin on both
    sides), or of the list, quote or float the picture is in. Pictures in
    tables keep their size, the table is measured with them. The setting also
    applies to pictures with width/height attributes, and to printing and
    export (HTMLM_Export, HTMLM_PrintBegin), with the text width of the page.

    Default is FALSE: pictures are shown in their size, as a browser does.
    TRUE suits Markdown documents, which often contain big screenshots
    without a size. When the gadget gets narrower or wider, the pictures are
    scaled again from the loaded picture; the scaled copy is kept until the
    size changes.

   SEE ALSO
    HTML_Margin
html.gadget/HTML_FixedFont                          html.gadget/HTML_FixedFont

   NAME
    HTML_FixedFont -- (struct TextAttr *) fixed width font (V1)

   USAGE
    (OM_NEW)

   FUNCTION
    Used for <pre>, <tt>, <code> ... Default: courier.font in the size
    nearest to the body text, or the system default font.
html.gadget/HTML_Font                                    html.gadget/HTML_Font

   NAME
    HTML_Font -- (struct TextAttr *) proportional base font (V1)

   USAGE
    (OM_NEW)

   FUNCTION
    Default: font of the default public screen. Headings and <font size>
    use other sizes of the same family, rounded to existing sizes.
html.gadget/HTML_Frame                                  html.gadget/HTML_Frame

